{"G3200":"<b> μεμβράνα</b>, ἡ, <br /> = Latin <i>membrāna</i>, <b>parchment</b>, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" NT.2Tim.4.13, 2nd c.AD(?): Charax Historicus 14, “POxy.” 2156.9 (4th-5th c.AD)\">NT+2nd c.AD+</a>]:—also <b>μέμβρανον</b>, τό, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 6th c.AD: Lydus, Joannes Laurentius Historicus “de Mensibus” 1.28 \">Refs 6th c.AD+</a>]: hence <i>adjective</i> <b>μεμβράϊνος</b>, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" “PMasp.” 144.6 (6th c.AD)\">Refs 6th c.AD+</a>], and <i>substantive</i> <b>μεμβραϊνάριος</b>, probably in [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" “Stud.Pal.” 20.194 (6th c.AD). \">Refs 6th c.AD+</a>]","G3201":"<b> μέμφομαι</b>, <br /> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 6th c.BC: Theognis Elegiacus 797, etc.\">Refs 6th c.BC+</a>]: <i>imperfect</i> ἐμέμφετο [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" Batrachomyomachia 70 \">Refs</a>]: <i>future</i> μέμψομαι [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 8th-7th c.BC: Hesiodus Epicus “Opera et Dies” 186, etc.\">Refs 8th c.BC+</a>]: <i>aorist</i> ἐμέμφθην [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 1.77, 3.13, 5th c.BC: Pindarus Lyricus “N.” 11.30 (κατα-), 5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Hippolytus” 1402, +others, 5th c.BC: Thucydides Historicus 4.85 (in _passive_ sense, 1st c.AD: Philo Judaeus 1.301, 2nd c.AD: Apollonius Dyscolus Grammaticus “de Syntaxi;” 67.22): but in _Attic dialect_ and Trag. commonly ἐμεμψάμην, as 4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Prometheus Vinctus” 1073 (_anapaest meter_), 5th-6th c.BC: Andocides Orator 4.3, 5th c.BC: Thucydides Historicus 1.143, also in 6th c.BC: Mimnermus Lyricus 14.5, 5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 2.24 \">Refs 6th c.BC+</a>]: <i>present</i> in <i>passive</i> sense, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 3rd c.AD(?): Diogenes Laertius 6.47, 2nd c.AD: Aspasius Philosophus “in Ethica Nicomachea commentaria - pars” 133.14: \">Refs 2nd c.AD+</a>]<i>future</i> μεμφθήσομαι Ps.-[<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 4th-3rd c.BC: Menander Comicus in Meineke “Fragm.Comedy texts Gr.” iv p.337 \">Refs 4th c.BC+</a>]:—<b>blame, censure</b>, first in [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 8th-7th c.BC: Hesiodus Epicus (though ἐπιμέμφομαι occurs in 8th c.BC: Homerus Epicus): \">Refs 8th c.BC+</a>]<br /><Level3><b>__1</b></Level3> with <i>accusative</i> <i>person</i>, μέμψονται δ᾽ ἄρα τούς [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 8th-7th c.BC: Hesiodus Epicus “Opera et Dies” 186, compare 6th c.BC: Theognis Elegiacus 797, 5th c.BC: Pindarus Lyricus “N.” 7.64, 5th c.BC: Sophocles Tragicus “Electra” 384, etc.; μ. τύχην 4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Prometheus Vinctus” 1073 (_anapaest meter_); μ. τὸν θέντα τὸν νόμον 5th-6th c.BC: Andocides Orator 4.3 \">Refs 8th c.BC+</a>]; κατὰ τὸ μαντήϊον οὐκ ὀρθῶς ὁ Κροῖσος μέμφεται (i.e. τὸν Λοξίαν) [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 1.91; μ. τινὰ πρὸς τοὺς φίλους 5th-6th c.BC: Xenophon Historicus “Oeconomicus” 11.23; μ. τινὰ εἴς τι [prev. author] “An.” 2.6.30. \">Refs 5th c.BC+</a>] <br /><Level4><b>__1.b</b></Level4> c.<i>accusative</i> <i>of things</i>, οἶνε, τὰ μέν σ᾽ αἰνῶ, τὰ δὲ μέμφομαι [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 6th c.BC: Theognis Elegiacus 873 \">Refs 6th c.BC+</a>]; μ. τὴν γνώμην, τὰ δῶρα, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 1.207, 3.13; μ. τὴν φιλοσοφίαν 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Euthydemus” 305b; ἄλλο οὐδὲν μ. 5th-6th c.BC: Xenophon Historicus “Anabasis” 7.6.39; μεμφθεὶς κατὰ τὸ πλῆθος τὸ ἑωυτοῦ στράτευμα 5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 1.77; ταῦτα.. προτ᾽ ἐμὸν θυμὸν ἐμεμψάμαν 3rd c.BC: Theocritus Poeta Bucolicus 30.24. \">Refs 5th c.BC+</a>]<br /><Level3><b>__2</b></Level3> with <i>dative</i> <i>person</i> et <i>accusative</i> <i>of things</i>, <b>impute as blameworthy, cast in one's teeth</b>, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 7th-6th c.BC: Sappho Lyrica “Papyrus fragments” in E. Diehl, 14.7 (probably), 5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 3.4, 4.180, 5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Nubes” 525, “Av.” 137, 5th c.BC: Thucydides Historicus 1.143, etc.: also with _accusative_ _cognate_, τῷ Λοξίᾳ μέμψιν μ. 5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Plutus” 10, etc.\">Refs 7th c.BC+</a>]; μ. τινὶ ὅτι.. [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 9.6, compare 6.92 \">Refs 5th c.BC+</a>]; οὕνεκα.. [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Helena” 31 \">Refs 5th c.BC+</a>]; εἰ.. [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th c.BC: Thucydides Historicus 4.85: with _dative_ _person_ et _genitive_ _of things_, οὔποτ᾽ ἀνδρὶ τῷδε κηρυκευμάτων μέμψει 4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Septem contra Thebas” 652:\">Refs 5th c.BC+</a>] with <i>genitive</i> <i>person</i> et <i>accusative</i> _of things_, ὃ μάλιστα μέμφονται ἡμῶν which is the chief <b>complaint they make</b> against us, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th c.BC: Thucydides Historicus 1.84. \">Refs 5th c.BC+</a>]<br /><Level3><b>__3</b></Level3> with <i>dative</i> <i>person</i> only, <b>to be dissatisfied with, find fault with</b>, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Septem contra Thebas” 560, “Pr.” 63, 5th c.BC: Sophocles Tragicus “Trachiniae” 470, 5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Orestes” 285, “IA” 899 (troch.), 5th-6th c.BC: Xenophon Historicus “Memorabilia” 3.5.20, NT.Heb.8.8 \">NT+5th c.BC+</a>]: with <i>participle</i> added, μ. ἡμῖν λογισαμένοις [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 2nd c.AD: Lucianus Sophista “Charid.” 20; ὡς κακῶς βουλευομένοις 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Phaedrus” 234b, compare “Cri.” 50d. \">Refs 5th c.BC+</a>]<br /><Level3><b>__4</b></Level3> with <i>genitive</i> <i>of things</i> only, <b>complain of</b>, οὐ μάχης.. μέμψει [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Fragmenta - American Journal of Philology” 199.3; εἴ τι μέμφῃ τῆς ἐμῆς ἀπουσίας 5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Hecuba” 962 \">Refs 5th c.BC+</a>]; τιμῆς ἐμέμφθη of her [neglected] honour [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\"compare (εὐχωλῆς ἐπιμέμφεται 8th c.BC: Ilias Homerus Epicus “Illiad” 1.93), 5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Hippolytus” 1402; μ. τῶν γεγενημένων 5th c.BC: Thucydides Historicus 8.109. \">Refs 8th c.BC+</a>]<br /><Level3><b>__5</b></Level3> with <i>infinitive</i> with μή, μ. μὴ πολλάκις βουλεύεσθαι <b>object</b> that one ought not.., [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" [prev. author] 3.42. \">Refs</a>]<br /><Level3><b>__6</b></Level3> <i>absolutely</i>, <b>find fault, complain</b>, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Supplices” 137 (Lyric poetry); ὅτι 4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Ethica Nicomachea” 1162b18. in Law, οἱ μεμφόμενοι\">Refs 4th c.BC+</a>] the <b>plaintiffs</b>, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" “GDI” 4998 (from Gortyn). \">Refs</a>]","G3202":"<b> μεμψῐ-μοιρος</b>, ον, <br /> <b>faultfinding, criticizing, querulous</b>, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th-6th c.BC: Isocrates Orator 12.8, 4th-3rd c.BC: Theophrastus Philosophus “Characteres” 17.2, 1st c.BC: Philodemus Philosophus “περὶ παρρησίας” p.42 O., NT.Jude.16, 2nd c.AD: Lucianus Sophista “Tim.” 13, etc.; τὸ μ. 1st-2nd c.AD: Plutarchus Biographus et Philosophus 2.50b \">NT+5th c.BC+</a>]: <i>comparative</i>, γυνὴ ἀνδρὸς -ότερον [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Historia Animalium” 608b10. \">Refs 4th c.BC+</a>]"}